{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai","id":418310,"title":"Can a Vampire/Kuei-jin fall in love with a Fera/Hengeyokai?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-24T20:50:27-08:00","id":418310,"title":"Can a Vampire/Kuei-jin fall in love with a Fera/Hengeyokai?","content":"I know they hate each other, but can such event happen or vice versa?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T21:04:12-08:00","id":418353,"title":"","content":"Maybe, but it's probably not going to get anywhere. Spirits won't like being around the vampire (only slightly less in the case of most Demon People), which is probably going to get the Changer to think long and hard about this whole star-crossed love thing and maybe consider that it isn't the best thing to keep up. Vampires, for their part, are generally callous and unfeeling by the standards of Changers that have Rage. Speaking of which, Rage - vampires might be slightly more likely to survive a frenzy, but if they hang around most Changers for very long, they're going to get unlucky. It's the same reason that Kinfolk are on edge most of the time when around werebeast relatives, lovers, spouses, children, etc. The odds go up if the vampire has Presence, since using it tends to trigger Rage rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T21:08:38-08:00","id":418359,"title":"","content":"Sure, they can fall in love, but there are plenty of potential problems. The biggest being the reaction of other Fera, which may try to kill our supernatural Romeo and Juliet. Vampires won't like it either, but are less likely to be directly violent over it. Ultimately, the romance is doomed, but then again so is any relationship between humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T21:47:40-08:00","id":418401,"title":"","content":"Don't the Fera see both as Wyrm-tainted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T22:16:57-08:00","id":418422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=418401#post418401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't the Fera see both as Wyrm-tainted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity 6 and lower pings to Sense Wyrm on the Kindred front. KotE Companion mentioned that the Demon People mostly ping to it all the time until they become Ancestor-ranked (i.e. 7+) to certain Dharmas, with Thrashing Dragons of sufficient enlightenment registering as Wyld creatures and Shining Ice Guardians as Weaver-ish (Devil Tigers are always Wyrm, all the time, and the strength just goes up). Presumably this would also include the Rising Phoenixes, who are simply seeking to live well, as &quot;acceptable&quot;, and in fact, that's about the only Dharma I could really see having a member getting anywhere with a Changer, since they have the capacity to walk around during the day for an unlimited amount of time by sealing their powers and essentially passing as mortal for a few hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T23:03:07-08:00","id":418438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=418353#post418353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, but it's probably not going to get anywhere. Spirits won't like being around the vampire (only slightly less in the case of most Demon People),</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not True for KJ. There's all sorts of good interaction with nonwyrm spirits among them. Thrashing Dragons and Cerulian veils explicitly have shaman types. Cranes and Godlings are required to act with spirits as part of their dharma, and Centipedes have all sorts of odd umbral interactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T23:51:23-08:00","id":418450,"title":"","content":"Everything else aside, the answer should be: yes. Love is an emotion both splats are capable of, technically.<br /> It would be complicated is all. But if that makes for a compelling story, have fun with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T01:34:24-08:00","id":418513,"title":"","content":"Are vampires capable of actual love, though? Or do they just like the novelty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T02:54:06-08:00","id":418549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=418513#post418513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are vampires capable of actual love, though? Or do they just like the novelty?</div> </div> </div> </div>The younger ones possibly but after seeing that loved one age and die the reality of their existence comes crashing down on them and then there are the some several hundred year elder the like to remember, but they probably just enjoy brief romance to remember what it was like to feel that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T04:26:33-08:00","id":418590,"title":"","content":"As long as there's love, yes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:14:05-08:00","id":418681,"title":"","content":"Why can't they? Other than they are enemies, there really is nothing in the rules that says they can't and if there was that is what the Golden Rule is truly all about. <br /> <br /> One of the most epic love stories in fiction are star crossed lovers. Stories of Garou and Kindred falling in love has been done for years and even a subject of some WoD Fiction Books (which Underworld ripped off).<br /> <br /> In Asian culture the idea of love is always tragic and always ends badly in their tales. Can bring some great drama to your game if that is the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:27:15-08:00","id":418700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=418353#post418353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, but it's probably not going to get anywhere. Spirits won't like being around the vampire (only slightly less in the case of most Demon People), which is probably going to get the Changer to think long and hard about this whole star-crossed love thing and maybe consider that it isn't the best thing to keep up. Vampires, for their part, are generally callous and unfeeling by the standards of Changers that have Rage. Speaking of which, Rage - vampires might be slightly more likely to survive a frenzy, but if they hang around most Changers for very long, they're going to get unlucky. It's the same reason that Kinfolk are on edge most of the time when around werebeast relatives, lovers, spouses, children, etc. The odds go up if the vampire has Presence, since using it tends to trigger Rage rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the ST some (or many) points in animalism may be of help here, it doesn't say that it does work on shapechangers but it wouldn't be unreasonable to assume that it does to some extent (just with a weakened effect). That may keep the vampire in question alive.<br /> There's also the old protean 6 which could force shapechangers back into their natural forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5027-dreyven","name":"Dreyven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:54:19-08:00","id":418796,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't they? Other than they are enemies, there really is nothing in the rules that says they can't and if there was that is what the Golden Rule is truly all about.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">One of the most epic love stories in fiction are star crossed lovers. Stories of Garou and Kindred falling in love has been done for years and even a subject of some WoD Fiction Books (which Underworld ripped off).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Classic WoD fiction is usually described - and quite reasonably - as &quot;canon on crack&quot;. No relationship with a vampire is considered healthy in the body of any classic WoD game, and werewolves generally have to put in massive amounts of work to be with beloved who are actually alive.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In Asian culture the idea of love is always tragic and always ends badly in their tales. Can bring some great drama to your game if that is the case.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>...I think that you're definitely making some hasty judgments based on skewed data there, to say nothing of vast amounts of unfavorable cultural lumping.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreyven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=418700#post418700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depending on the ST some (or many) points in animalism may be of help here, it doesn't say that it does work on shapechangers but it wouldn't be unreasonable to assume that it does to some extent (just with a weakened effect). That may keep the vampire in question alive.<br /> There's also the old protean 6 which could force shapechangers back into their natural forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's quite reasonable to assume that Animalism doesn't work because the books say, explicitly, that Animalism doesn't work on Changers unless it's a power that also works on Kindred or other monsters. So you can provoke frenzies at higher ratings (5+), but not stop them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:57:55-08:00","id":419762,"title":"","content":"Funny, my overall impression was that interactions between the Wan Kuei and the Shapeshifters were less acrimonious and automatically &quot;wyrm, wyrm, wyrm, kill, kill, kill!!&quot; than in Europa and the Americas...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T20:14:47-08:00","id":419767,"title":"","content":"I'd say having the Fera lover frenzy and attack the vampire would be a case of the Storyteller being a jerk (assuming the lovers are player characters) unless the conditions were very specific. A werewolf with a Rage below 4 can't even frenzy unless there are unusual circumstances, they can also spend Willpower to come out of the frenzy. <br /> <br /> I'd say the bigger problem for both is other Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T20:32:37-08:00","id":419776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=419762#post419762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny, my overall impression was that interactions between the Wan Kuei and the Shapeshifters were less acrimonious and automatically &quot;wyrm, wyrm, wyrm, kill, kill, kill!!&quot; than in Europa and the Americas...</div> </div> </div> </div>That was how it was, but it seems kind of like it's up in the air right now. There are a few things that the 20th Anniversary Editions seem to be shaking up, and anything involving KotE could be it. Hard to tell if the Okuma writeup with the Demon People existing before they fell is an error or an intentional change right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'd say having the Fera lover frenzy and attack the vampire would be a case of the Storyteller being a jerk (assuming the lovers are player characters) unless the conditions were very specific. A werewolf with a Rage below 4 can't even frenzy unless there are unusual circumstances, they can also spend Willpower to come out of the frenzy. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'd say the bigger problem for both is other Fera.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unusual circumstances pretty much describes a Garou or Fera being in love with a vampire. Expect more of them to follow you around and push your Rage up to the necessary level. Also, is the ST also a jerk if unusual circumstances end up causing the changer character to frenzy and kill another character? Because that sort of thing isn't exactly uncommon in Werewolf. It's part of why they don't always get along with anything - &quot;We have this vital objective and you absolutely shouldn't go on a ramp... oh, too late.&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T20:42:29-08:00","id":419777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=419776#post419776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unusual circumstances pretty much describes a Garou or Fera being in love with a vampire. Expect more of them to follow you around and push your Rage up to the necessary level. Also, is the ST also a jerk if unusual circumstances end up causing the changer character to frenzy and kill another character? Because that sort of thing isn't exactly uncommon in Werewolf. It's part of why they don't always get along with anything - &quot;We have this vital objective and you absolutely shouldn't go on a ramp... oh, too late.&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It is an unusual circumstance, but it doesn't increase Rage or cause frenzy rolls. If the ST just decides to make your character roll frenzy, then I would say that they are being a jerk. I mean, with werewolves with high Rage, those things can happen, Thrall of the Wyrm and all, but I don't see it as a bigger concern in this case than in any other situation. Remember, a Rage below 4, which is a fair number of Fera, can't even frenzy under most circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T20:54:41-08:00","id":419783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=419777#post419777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an unusual circumstance, but it doesn't increase Rage or cause frenzy rolls. If the ST just decides to make your character roll frenzy, then I would say that they are being a jerk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing that isn't what we were talking about. Refer to the seduction rules for the little end note about having to roll Rage if the character gets too passionate, and consider how packmates or other close associates attacking you on account of your horrid, undead abomination of a lover might sour someone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, with werewolves with high Rage, those things can happen, Thrall of the Wyrm and all, but I don't see it as a bigger concern in this case than in any other situation. Remember, a Rage below 4, which is a fair number of Fera, can't even frenzy under most circumstances. </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really matter, because getting in between Changers and Vampires is a good way to get people who will push your buttons to scuttle out of the woodwork under both sides the moment something comes up. Any sun-aligned Changers might also suffer horribly just for spending so much time around the vampire while not trying to kill it; refer to Sunbane from the Mokole Breedbook.<br /> <br /> This is assuming that the vampire doesn't return to the love nest hungry one day and attack the changer... which is liable to end badly, and can be engineered by the political enemies, with which most vampires are lousy like a century-old mattress in a derelict building.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T19:27:46-08:00","id":420991,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Saur Ops Specialist;n418796]<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Classic WoD fiction is usually described - and quite reasonably - as &quot;canon on crack&quot;. No relationship with a vampire is considered healthy in the body of any classic WoD game, and werewolves generally have to put in massive amounts of work to be with beloved who are actually alive.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Vancouver Dark Alliance, Under A Blood Red Moon </b>and <b>Milwaukee</b><b> By Night </b>are examples it is mentioned. Oh wait they are Game Modules. So sorry. Seriously? What about the idea of Vampire Companion Merit from 1st Edition to what is the general one called Supernatural Companion. <br /> <br /> Even the <b>Storyteller Guides </b>talk about this and doing it. <br /> <br /> There are no official rules on not doing it either. It is all flavor and what is up to what the Storyteller wants to do and the Players. Are you saying a Werewolf whose Kin Folk was turned to a Vampire would not still love him/her? <br /> <br /> It is all theme and thought in the game. Your thing about the difficulties of holding a relationship with someone being a Vampire or a Werewolf regardless if they are with a mortal or not is a big part of the Social play in WoD. Balancing who and what you are as a monster and human. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T21:17:16-08:00","id":421198,"title":"","content":"hey, if a zombie looking teenager can make a 100 year old virgin sparkling vampire, and a boy with the face of a llama fall inlove with her. i dont see why shoudnt this be possible.<br /> <br /> Worst case Scenario: Twilight<br /> Best Case Scenario: Romeo and Juliet..but more gorey","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T23:21:23-08:00","id":421366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=420991#post420991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Vancouver Dark Alliance, Under A Blood Red Moon </b>and <b>Milwaukee</b><b> By Night </b>are examples it is mentioned. Oh wait they are Game Modules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see them in the same light as Rage Across Australia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So sorry. Seriously? What about the idea of Vampire Companion Merit from 1st Edition to what is the general one called Supernatural Companion. </div> </div> </div>Yes, what about it? It got axed in Player's Guide to the Garou, presumably because you just pay more Ally points for it. It also points out that it can backfire horribly on you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even the <b>Storyteller Guides </b>talk about this and doing it.<br /> <br /> There are no official rules on not doing it either. It is all flavor and what is up to what the Storyteller wants to do and the Players. Are you saying a Werewolf whose Kin Folk was turned to a Vampire would not still love him/her? </div> </div> </div>Well, there are rules. Again, Renown loss. As for vampire kin, congratulations! You get to watch as the person you loved slowly dies and rots on the inside, becoming a danger to everything said kin probably held dear. The only moral course for a vampire is to walk out into the sun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is all theme and thought in the game. Your thing about the difficulties of holding a relationship with someone being a Vampire or a Werewolf regardless if they are with a mortal or not is a big part of the Social play in WoD. Balancing who and what you are as a monster and human. </div> </div> </div>Werewolf and Vampire have two different balancing acts that tend to be incompatible. Sure, it adds conflict to make things interesting, but the relationship is ultimately doomed from the start. Don't expect any other outcome. In fact, if you keep piling on the difficulties, it goes from interesting to a train wreck. So, all in all, not something you'd want to be doing regularly. Seems like it would drain the players significantly to go through with a game like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T04:24:57-08:00","id":421580,"title":"","content":"As mentioned before: it is possible. However, I see it like it's real world equivalent: multiracial couple in a less tolerant country/culture/era...but with Rage fuelled/Blood frenzying friends, family and neighbors. It possible, but it has the potential of becoming really ugly qui te fast.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer:<br /> 1) I'm sorry if the analogy hurts/offends anyone and if the moderator feel it needs to be removed, I will accept their decision.<br /> 2) I have personally experienced this to a certain extend in South Korea: I was married to a Korean woman and I'm a white Canadian. The marriage failed eventually but for other reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T05:57:11-08:00","id":421646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=421366#post421366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see them in the same light as Rage Across Australia.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, what about it? It got axed in Player's Guide to the Garou, presumably because you just pay more Ally points for it. It also points out that it can backfire horribly on you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, there are rules. Again, Renown loss. As for vampire kin, congratulations! You get to watch as the person you loved slowly dies and rots on the inside, becoming a danger to everything said kin probably held dear. The only moral course for a vampire is to walk out into the sun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Werewolf and Vampire have two different balancing acts that tend to be incompatible. Sure, it adds conflict to make things interesting, but the relationship is ultimately doomed from the start. Don't expect any other outcome. In fact, if you keep piling on the difficulties, it goes from interesting to a train wreck. So, all in all, not something you'd want to be doing regularly. Seems like it would drain the players significantly to go through with a game like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you actually play the game or do you just ROLL Play? WoD is giant tragedy. This is not D&amp;D where everything ends in happy endings. WoD is a personal horror game from the get go. It has been described in all the books.<br /> <br /> Player's Guide to the Garou did not Axe Supernatural Companion and it is still in W20. Check the Revised book.<br /> <br /> Whole idea of tragic love affair is one of the many aspects of the game.<br /> <br /> I ran a Mage game for about 2 years and in the end the players discovered they were captured by the Technocracy and were all brains in jars. That was such a happy ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","user":"Nene Richards","date":". 02-27-2015, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T10:59:50-08:00","id":421955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=421646#post421646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do you actually play the game or do you just ROLL Play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! I have not heard that one in ages. I thought that the sentiment died out in the oughts, and the early oughts at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WoD is giant tragedy. This is not D&amp;D where everything ends in happy endings. WoD is a personal horror game from the get go. It has been described in all the books. </div> </div> </div>Thus, draining by definition, with some elements being even more draining, when hard work doesn't even manage to do anything. Also, if you're familiar with W20, you should know about a little thing called the Eighth Sign of the Phoenix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Player's Guide to the Garou did not Axe Supernatural Companion and it is still in W20. Check the Revised book. </div> </div> </div>And they also switched the Umbra around in ways that really screw up how the Mokole dealt with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whole idea of tragic love affair is one of the many aspects of the game.<br /> <br /> I ran a Mage game for about 2 years and in the end the players discovered they were captured by the Technocracy and were all brains in jars. That was such a happy ending. </div> </div> </div>There are different play styles. Some people like to have that kind of Shymalanian twist. Others like transparency. We're not the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T02:55:39-08:00","id":422759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=421646#post421646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WoD is a personal horror game from the get go. It has been described in all the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The WoD is not one game, and the constituent games do not have the same themes or deal with horror. Crossing them over will cause its own pain, and playing star crossed lovers won't end well if you play up the core principles of the games. If you don't it's down to you and your players and what you want to play, and that's fine.<br /> <br /> But I do find it hillarious how you're saying how star crossed lovers can work out and then ending the point by saying all the WoD games are supposed to end terribly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:18:30-08:00","id":424125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai#post418310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know they hate each other, but can such event happen or vice versa?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't a question of hate. It is a fundamental matter of supernatural hormones. Consider any time you have met someone who just gave you a bad vibe. I once heard a psychiatrist state that she did not believe in God, but when she met Jeffrey Dahmer for the first time she felt some energy she could only describe as &quot;palpable evil&quot;. Consider the chills that run one's spine in those brief weird instantaneous flashes in the dark abandoned places. Further, no known primate fails to make distinctions between members of its same species based on color patterns. These patterns set their bands/troupes apart. Often forced sharing of territory and resources results in violence to drive out the interlopers. Consider the results of this instinct in the actions of prejudice in the more civilized and developed of these species - man.<br /> <br /> While the Romeo and Juliet story is a wonderful tragedy - it is still a tragedy where intolerance exists in members of the same species, cultural outlook, and language. The very world view of Shifters, who denounce humans as prey because that is cannibalism, opposes the Vampiric nature wherein humans are prey. A wolf pup might play with a faun, but in the end one is predator and one is food - the momentary frolic will not last.<br /> <br /> To say they hate each other is to misrepresent the condition. It is like saying a solar system has a mild allergy to a black hole 100,000 light years in diameter. (That is by the way the size of our galaxy.) All vampires exude the corruption of the Wyrm. All ghosts radiate the corruption of the Wyrm. Their existence is not merely unlife, it is antithetical to the existence of the living. For the shifters, agents of the living Gaia, manifestations of Life in its fiercest defense of self the presence is intolerable no matter how good a guy the vampire might seem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 03-01-2015, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:06:23-08:00","id":424410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All vampires exude the corruption of the Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>Not all. High Humanity Vampires do not and in some sources neither do those high in the Road of the Beast/Path of Feral Heart similarly of the Hungry Dead the Cranes do not nor do some of the Dragons or Centipedes especially those who are advanced in their Dharmas. So again no.<br /> <br /> Such a love story is possible, love is funny that way, but it has a good chance of turning into a tragedy for multiple reasons, one possibility is that the lovers end up killing one another in Frenzy but that is actually pretty unlikely, but it is possible. It is more likely with a shifter and a Hungry Dead as they have a lot better relations than shifters and the Kindred do, and the eastern shifters know that despite it all the Hungry Dead do have a purpose under Heaven so it is not indiscriminate hatred between them tho said relations are still tense to say the least. Still a romance between a Dragon and a shifter could even be tolerated at least as long as the shifter courts and the dead courts manage to hold a truce between themselves, though if that union would produce a child it could make things a lot tenser to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:12:18-08:00","id":424415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=424410#post424410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all. High Humanity Vampires do not and in some sources neither do those high in the Road of the Beast/Path of Feral Heart similarly of the Hungry Dead the Cranes do not nor do some of the Dragons or Centipedes especially those who are advanced in their Dharmas. So again no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, wraiths don't ping on Sense Wyrm until their Shadow's Angst is greater than the Psyche's Willpower rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:34:15-08:00","id":424428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=424410#post424410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Accepted. Logical fallacy on my part. However, certainly most vampires will seam Wyrm tainted to the shifting breeds - and even if they don't seem that way to the senses, they will be defined that way by their upbringing. A Ronin or one that is already tainted has a shot at a relationship, one full of self-loathing, doubt, and the gnawing wyrm of disgust in the back of their brain. As for the Eastern Courts, I am less familiar with them. The Western shifters were already complicated enough that I never wanted to play them, (only read all their lore).<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:20:03-08:00","id":424506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/418310-can-a-vampire-kuei-jin-fall-in-love-with-a-fera-hengeyokai?p=424428#post424428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Accepted. Logical fallacy on my part. However, certainly most vampires will seam Wyrm tainted to the shifting breeds - and even if they don't seem that way to the senses, they will be defined that way by their upbringing. A Ronin or one that is already tainted has a shot at a relationship, one full of self-loathing, doubt, and the gnawing wyrm of disgust in the back of their brain. As for the Eastern Courts, I am less familiar with them. The Western shifters were already complicated enough that I never wanted to play them, (only read all their lore).<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Members of the Beast Courts remember well the treachery of the Demon People in getting them to turn on each other (which killed the Okuma down to the last), so while they might deal with them non-homicidally more often, they're probably even less likely to trust the returned hellborn souls than Garou and Fera from outside their culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T02:57:09-08:00","id":431161,"title":"","content":"Some of the most tragic and epic stories in our history revolved around two people being in love no matter the circumstances or repercussions. And I'd bet at least a few people here were involved with someone in their past they should not have, or where it was discriminated against. I'll never forget the weeks long fight I had with my mother over the skin color of a girlfriend in high school.<br /> <br /> People fall for each other, even when it's wrong or forbidden. To say that dynamic wouldn't exist in a make believe world based upon our own seems just silly. In addition to that these relationships exist in the modules, the books, etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4579-skeleton-jack","name":"Skeleton Jack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T09:15:42-07:00","id":461091,"title":"","content":"If the vampire and werewolf are still new to their existences (freshly changed / embraced), I could see it as a possibility, since they're still mostly human in their mindset. Kuei Jin, however, I'm not so sure. When they first come back to life, they're mindless animals devouring human flesh. They need the help of their fellow Kuei Jin to regain their minds, and that means assimilating into Kuei Jin philosophy.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's confirmed (though rare) that different supernaturals have joined forces together, so I don't see why they can't form relationships too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-29-2015, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T10:15:39-07:00","id":461157,"title":"","content":"Actually some Kuei-Jin have the strength of will to return in control, not many of them but some. And among the Kuei-Jin risen outside of the Far East there are k\u00e0nbuji\u00e0n, Kuei-Jin that weren't found by their kind but overcame their P'o and develop their own personal path tied to one of the five Virtues, Hun, P'o, Yin, Yang and Balance, to sustain them. And Anarchs Unbound revealed that there are young Kuei-Jin in the Movement, undoubtedly there are k\u00e0nbuji\u00e0n among them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T13:23:09-07:00","id":461385,"title":"","content":"It's not that they cannot fall in love. It's just that it's bloody unlikely, and it will end bloody for both of them. It's harder to imagine the milleau in which it might be plausible for them to interact in a way which will draw them to each other. With the wary diplomacy between Kuei Jin and Hengeyokai I can actually see something blossoming there sooner then among the Kindred and the Fera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:41:09-07:00","id":462643,"title":"","content":"Love is easy enough to happen and hard enough to control. The question is... what do they do about it? If the KJ isn't on Thrashing Dragons does the Fera Push here there? With Kindred does the Fera perform one last right of clensing on her beloved while he's staked in the ground to save his soul? Does the Kindred who wants her love to last forever damn her lover to Abominationhood? Love can lead to all sorts of horrific places... just ask Devil Homura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}